#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:3
msgid "Debugging Your Application"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:11
msgid "Checking Logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:16
msgid "CodeIgniter Error Logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:18
msgid ""
"CodeIgniter logs error messages, according to the settings in "
"**app/Config/Logger.php**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:20
msgid ""
"The default configuration has daily log files stored in "
"**writable/logs**. It would be a good idea to check them if things aren't"
" working the way you expect!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:23
msgid ""
"You can adjust the error threshold to see more or fewer messages. See "
":ref:`Logging <logging-configuration>` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:27
msgid "Logging All SQL Queries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:29
msgid ""
"All SQL queries issued by CodeIgniter can be logged. See :ref:`Database "
"Events <database-events-dbquery>` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:34
msgid "Replacing var_dump()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:36
msgid ""
"While using Xdebug and a good IDE can be indispensable to debug your "
"application, sometimes a quick ``var_dump()`` is all you need. "
"CodeIgniter makes that even better by bundling in the excellent `Kint "
"<https://kint-php.github.io/kint/>`_ debugging tool for PHP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:41
msgid ""
"This goes way beyond your usual tool, providing many alternate pieces of "
"data, like formatting timestamps into recognizable dates, showing you "
"hexcodes as colors, display array data like a table for easy reading, and"
" much, much more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:46
msgid "Enabling Kint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:48
msgid ""
"By default, Kint is enabled in **development** and **testing** "
":doc:`environments </general/environments>` only. It will be enabled "
"whenever the constant ``CI_DEBUG`` is defined and its value is truthy. "
"This is defined in the boot files (e.g. "
"**app/Config/Boot/development.php**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:53
msgid "Using Kint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:56
msgid "d()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:58
msgid ""
"The ``d()`` method dumps all of the data it knows about the contents "
"passed as the only parameter to the screen, and allows the script to "
"continue executing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:65
msgid "dd()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:67
msgid ""
"This method is identical to ``d()``, except that it also ``die()`` and no"
" further code is executed this request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:70
msgid "trace()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:72
msgid ""
"This provides a backtrace to the current execution point, with Kint's own"
" unique spin:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:77
msgid ""
"For more information, see `Kint's page <https://kint-"
"php.github.io/kint//>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:83
msgid "The Debug Toolbar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:85
msgid ""
"The Debug Toolbar provides at-a-glance information about the current page"
" request, including benchmark results, queries you have run, request and "
"response data, and more. This can all prove very useful during "
"development to help you debug and optimize."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:89
msgid ""
"The Debug Toolbar is still under construction with several planned "
"features not yet implemented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:92
msgid "Enabling the Toolbar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:94
msgid ""
"The toolbar is enabled by default in any :doc:`environment "
"</general/environments>` *except* **production**. It will be shown "
"whenever the constant ``CI_DEBUG`` is defined and its value is truthy. "
"This is defined in the boot files (e.g. "
"**app/Config/Boot/development.php**) and can be modified there to "
"determine what environment to show."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:98
msgid ""
"The Debug Toolbar is not displayed when your ``baseURL`` setting (in "
"**app/Config/App.php** or ``app.baseURL`` in **.env**) does not match "
"your actual URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:100
msgid ""
"The toolbar itself is displayed as an :doc:`After Filter "
"</incoming/filters>`. You can stop it from ever running by removing "
"``'toolbar'`` from the ``$required`` (or ``$globals``) property of "
"**app/Config/Filters.php**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:103
msgid "Prior to v4.5.0, the toolbar was set to ``$globals`` by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:106
msgid "Choosing What to Show"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:108
msgid ""
"CodeIgniter ships with several Collectors that, as the name implies, "
"collect data to display on the toolbar. You can easily make your own to "
"customize the toolbar. To determine which collectors are shown, again "
"head over to the **app/Config/Toolbar.php** configuration file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:114
msgid ""
"Comment out any collectors that you do not want to show. Add custom "
"Collectors here by providing the fully-qualified class name. The exact "
"collectors that appear here will affect which tabs are shown, as well as "
"what information is shown on the Timeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:118
msgid ""
"Some tabs, like Database and Logs, will only display when they have "
"content to show. Otherwise, they are removed to help out on smaller "
"displays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:121
msgid "The Collectors that ship with CodeIgniter are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:123
msgid ""
"**Timers** collects all of the benchmark data, both by the system and by "
"your application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:124
msgid ""
"**Database** Displays a list of queries that all database connections "
"have performed, and their execution time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:125
msgid ""
"**Logs** Any information that was logged will be displayed here. In long-"
"running systems, or systems with many items being logged, this can cause "
"memory issues and should be disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:126
msgid ""
"**Views** Displays render time for views on the timeline, and shows any "
"data passed to the views on a separate tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:127
msgid ""
"**Cache** Will display information about cache hits and misses, and "
"execution times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:128
msgid ""
"**Files** displays a list of all files that have been loaded during this "
"request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:129
msgid ""
"**Routes** displays information about the current route and all routes "
"defined in the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:130
msgid ""
"**Events** displays a list of all events that have been loaded during "
"this request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:133
msgid "Setting Benchmark Points"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:135
msgid ""
"In order for the Profiler to compile and display your benchmark data you "
"must name your mark points using specific syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:137
msgid ""
"Please read the information on setting Benchmark points in the "
":doc:`Benchmark Library </testing/benchmark>` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:140
msgid "Creating Custom Collectors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:142
msgid ""
"Creating custom collectors is a straightforward task. You create a new "
"class, fully-namespaced so that the autoloader can locate it, that "
"extends ``CodeIgniter\\Debug\\Toolbar\\Collectors\\BaseCollector``. This "
"provides a number of methods that you can override, and has four required"
" class properties that you must correctly set depending on how you want "
"the Collector to work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:149
msgid ""
"**$hasTimeline** should be set to ``true`` for any Collector that wants "
"to display information in the toolbar's timeline. If this is true, you "
"will need to implement the ``formatTimelineData()`` method to format and "
"return the data for display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:153
msgid ""
"**$hasTabContent** should be ``true`` if the Collector wants to display "
"its own tab with custom content. If this is true, you will need to "
"provide a ``$title``, implement the ``display()`` method to render out "
"tab's contents, and might need to implement the ``getTitleDetails()`` "
"method if you want to display additional information just to the right of"
" the tab content's title."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:158
msgid ""
"**$hasVarData** should be ``true`` if this Collector wants to add "
"additional data to the ``Vars`` tab. If this is true, you will need to "
"implement the ``getVarData()`` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:161
msgid "**$title** is displayed on open tabs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:164
msgid "Displaying a Toolbar Tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:166
msgid "To display a toolbar tab you must:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:168
msgid ""
"Fill in ``$title`` with the text displayed as both the toolbar title and "
"the tab header."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:169
msgid "Set ``$hasTabContent`` to ``true``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:170
msgid "Implement the ``display()`` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:171
msgid "Optionally, implement the ``getTitleDetails()`` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:173
msgid ""
"The ``display()`` creates the HTML that is displayed within the tab "
"itself. It does not need to worry about the title of the tab, as that is "
"automatically handled by the toolbar. It should return a string of HTML."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:176
msgid ""
"The ``getTitleDetails()`` method should return a string that is displayed"
" just to the right of the tab's title. it can be used to provide "
"additional overview information. For example, the Database tab displays "
"the total number of queries across all connections, while the Files tab "
"displays the total number of files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:181
msgid "Providing Timeline Data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:183
msgid "To provide information to be displayed in the Timeline you must:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:185
msgid "Set ``$hasTimeline`` to ``true``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:186
msgid "Implement the ``formatTimelineData()`` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:188
msgid ""
"The ``formatTimelineData()`` method must return an array of arrays "
"formatted in a way that the timeline can use it to sort it correctly and "
"display the correct information. The inner arrays must include the "
"following information:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:194
msgid "Providing Vars"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:196
msgid "To add data to the Vars tab you must:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:198
msgid "Set ``$hasVarData`` to ``true``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:199
msgid "Implement ``getVarData()`` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:201
msgid ""
"The ``getVarData()`` method should return an array containing arrays of "
"key/value pairs to display. The name of the outer array's key is the name"
" of the section on the Vars tab:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:209
msgid "Hot Reloading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:213
msgid ""
"The Debug Toolbar includes a feature called Hot Reloading that allows you"
" to make changes to your application's code and have them automatically "
"reloaded in the browser without having to refresh the page. This is a "
"great time-saver during development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:215
msgid ""
"To enable Hot Reloading while you are developing, you can click the "
"button on the left side of the toolbar that looks like a refresh icon. "
"This will enable Hot Reloading for all pages until you disable it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:217
msgid ""
"Hot Reloading works by scanning the files within the **app** directory "
"every second and looking for changes. If it finds any, it will send a "
"message to the browser to reload the page. It does not scan any other "
"directories, so if you are making changes to files outside of the **app**"
" directory, you will need to manually refresh the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/debugging.rst:219
msgid ""
"If you need to watch files outside of the **app** directory, or are "
"finding it slow due to the size of your project, you can specify the "
"directories to scan and the file extensions to scan for in the "
"``$watchedDirectories`` and ``$watchedExtensions`` properties of the "
"**app/Config/Toolbar.php** configuration file."
msgstr ""

